+
+    fix: anchor gitleaks sk-api-key regex to non-alnum boundary (BT-83)
+    
+    The sk-api-key rule in .gitleaks.toml matched the sk- substring mid-word,
+    causing tier1 secrets FAIL on board prose like 'verdict=none:task-complete-unavailable'
+    (token length 23, matched at tasks.jsonl:198). The judge misattributed the
+    finding to .gitreins/** harness state; the actual finding was board prose,
+    and the allowlist already covers .gitreins/.
+    
+    Fix: prefix the regex with (?:^|[^a-zA-Z0-9]) (RE2-safe, no lookbehind).
+    Add internal/secretscheck regression test pinning both sides: mid-word
+    prose no longer matches, boundary-delimited 20+ char sk- tokens still do,
+    the 20-char minimum still holds, and the anchor shape is enforced
+    structurally so a future silent drop is caught.
+    
+    Addresses BT-83.
+    
+    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
